{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_IDSM_SECTION_7_8_Reporting_and_Persistence_of_SEVs","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_IntrusionDetectionSystemManager","page":35,"text":"7.8 Reporting and Persistence of SEVs\nOnce the filter chain has processed the incoming SEvs, the resulting events from the processing filter chain are considered QSEvs. Only QSEvs are further handled by the on-board IDS. These QSEvs can be either persisted in memory, sent to another ECU, or both depending on the configuration. The destination of a QSEv is called data sink. Manager","caption":"7.8 Reporting and Persistence of SEVs","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_IDSM_SECTION_7_8_Reporting_and_Persistence_of_SEVs","releases":["R23-11"],"page":35,"hash":"74abdfe9e55ff3bf","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/77e95e5e04ab/page_35.webp"}],"releases":["R23-11"],"screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/77e95e5e04ab/page_35.webp","trel":"R23-11","tstat":"section","drop":"R24-11","kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"ARCHITECTURAL_CONTEXT","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"forwarding QSEvs to data sinks","rel":[],"id":"SWS_IdsM_00910"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"ARCHITECTURAL_CONTEXT","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"forwarding QSEvs to other ECUs","rel":[],"id":"SWS_IdsM_01202"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"ARCHITECTURAL_CONTEXT","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"persisting on-board QSEvs in memory","rel":[],"id":"SWS_IdsM_01600"}],"ok":true,"schema":"versions-explorer@1"}